	<TR>

	<TD COLSPAN="4" WIDTH="500"><FONT FACE="Arial, Helvetica" SIZE="-1">To offer the most support to its members, The Guild is organized in a hierarchical structure:<BR><BR>

<B>Ambassadors Emeritus</B> - The Ambassadors Emeritus consist of Guild members who have contributed the most to the guild over the longest period of time.  With no formal responsibilities, the Ambassadors Emeritus are those to whom the HPA owes the deepest thanks, appreciation, and respect.  The Ambassadors Emeritus contribute to overall guild events through their general participation, and though without voting responsibilities, informally contribute to the overall direction of the Guild along with the High Council.<BR><BR>

<B>The High Council</B> - The High Planes Ambassadors are administered by a High Council, or "Round Table", of its most active members in longest standing, no one member taking precedence over any other. Each having a designated office, The High Council is responsible for organizing and carrying through the major services that support the Guild in general.  In addition, their responsibilities include writing policy, recruiting, hearing and working through member-offered suggestions, resolving disputes, and appointing The Group Leaders (Council).<BR><BR>

<B>Group Leaders (Council)</B> - The Council consists of Group Leaders from each of our four class groups.  The Group Leaders are responsible for being a general supportive and informative resource for the members in their class groups; overseeing class and group-specific training issues; helping coordinate quest and equipment acquisition; resolution of minor disputes; appointment of Group Officers; and are consulted on guild-wide policy issues.<BR><BR>

<B>Group Officers</B> - Each Group has a Group Officer who assists the Group Leaders.  The Group Officers' responsibilities include helping others in their Group; running Guild Mules; and generally being supportive members for their Group and the Guild.<BR><BR>

<B>Class Groups</B> - Guild members primarily turn to any of their Group Officers or Group Leaders for suppport.<BR><BR>

<B>Recruiters</B> - Not a part of the main hierarchy, Recruiters are responsible for bringing new members into the guild.  Recruiters are appointed by the High Council, and may also simultaneously be a ranking officer within the guild.</FONT></TD></TR>
	<TR><TD COLSPAN="4" WIDTH="500"><IMG SRC="/img/pix.gif" WIDTH="1" HEIGHT="10"></TD></TR>
</TABLE>
